  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Economy Facility - Phase 2</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Green Economy Fazilit&#xe4;t - Vorratspr&#xfc;fungsteil</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Mit diesem Vorhaben soll ein Beitrag geleistet werden, das wirtschaftliche Wachstum Ser-biens vom Verbrauch und der Verschmutzung nat&#xfc;rlicher Ressourcen und vom Aussto&#xdf; von Treibhausgasen zu entkoppeln und Serbien auf dem Weg hin zu einer Green Economy zu unterst&#xfc;tzen.Zielsetzung ist es, &#xfc;ber eine FZ-Kreditlinie das Kreditangebot des serbischen Bankensektors f&#xfc;r Investitionen zu erweitern, die zu Energieeinsparungen, Verringerung von Schadstoffemissionen und/oder einer Reduzierung des Ressourcenverbrauchs f&#xfc;hren. Die &#xfc;ber die FZ-Kreditlinie refinanzierten Green Economy Loans bzw. Umweltkredite sollen kleinsten, kleinen und mittleren Unternehmen (KKMU), &#xf6;ffentlichen Versorgungsunternehmen und Kommunen zur Verf&#xfc;gung gestellt werden und somit deren Zugang zu mittel- bis langfristiger Finanzierung f&#xfc;r Investitionsvorhaben mit positiver Umweltwirkung verbessern.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is intended to contribute to decoupling Serbias economic growth from the consumption and pollution of natural resources and the emission of greenhouse gases and to support Serbia on its way to a green economy.The aim is to use an FC credit line to expand the Serbian banking sectors range of credit for investments that lead to energy savings, the reduction of pollutant emissions and/or a reduction in resource consumption. The Green Economy Loans or environmental loans refinanced via the FC credit line are intended to be made available to micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSME), public utility companies and municipalities, thus improving their access to medium- to long-term financing for investment projects with a positive environmental impact.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Refinanzierung von umweltbewu&#xdf;ten und energieeffizienten Investitionen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is intended to contribute to decoupling Serbias economic growth from the consumption and pollution of natural resources and the emission of greenhouse gases and to support Serbia on its way to a green economy.The aim is to use an FC credit line to expand the Serbian banking sectors range of credit for investments that lead to energy savings, the reduction of pollutant emissions and/or a reduction in resource consumption. The Green Economy Loans or environmental loans refinanced via the FC credit line are intended to be made available to micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSME), public utility companies and municipalities, thus improving their access to medium- to long-term financing for investment projects with a positive environmental impact.</narrative>
  </description>
